differently, the reading that better protects the copyright holder applies)

1. Free use (personal learning only). An individual may download, install and run the
   unmodified Software and read its source free of charge, only if (a) the use is solely
   for that individual's own learning, including a student's own assignments and
   self-study, (b) no money or other economic benefit is obtained from the use directly or
   indirectly, and (c) this license and the copyright notice are kept intact.
1-2. Educational use that requires a purchased license or prior written permission.
   Companies, private academies, universities, educational institutions and organizations
   must buy a license or obtain written permission before using the Software in classes,
   courses, curricula, practice sessions, teaching materials or demonstrations, whatever
   the subject (vision AI, artificial intelligence, video generation, data analysis, etc.),
   when (a) the teaching is funded by the state, local governments or public bodies
   (government-funded or vocational training, commissioned public education), (b) students
   pay tuition, course, enrolment or material fees directly or indirectly, or (c) any
   organization rather than an individual uses it as part of its work or curriculum.
   Instructors or students in these settings cannot rely on section 1.
2. Prohibited without prior written permission: (a) any commercial use, (b) modification,
   adaptation, extraction, combination, translation or other derivative works, (c)
   redistribution of the original or any modified version, or inclusion in another product
   or service, (d) offering the Software as a remote service.
3. GitHub Terms of Service. Viewing and forking within GitHub as allowed by the GitHub Terms
   of Service are not restricted by this license; using, modifying or redistributing a fork
   beyond section 1 remains prohibited by section 2.
4. Licenses and permission for section 1-2 use, any other use beyond section 1,
   modification, redistribution or commercial use are requested from the copyright holder
   (https://github.com/KORBrianLee). Without explicit written permission or a license
   agreement, permission is not granted.
5. (a) Third-party components (model weights, runtimes, libraries, FFmpeg) are not covered and
   keep their own licenses (docs/MODEL_LICENSES.md, docs/licenses/). Where both apply,
   comply with the stricter terms. (b) The use-based restrictions of every model the Software
   downloads or runs (Attachment A of the LTX-Video Open Weights License, Attachment A of the
   CreativeML Open RAIL-M, the Qualcomm Responsible AI License, the Skywork Community License
   and the like) are part of    this license and bind the user; a use that violates them breaches
   this license. A purchased license or permission under this license does not include any
   model license; in particular, organisations with annual revenues of USD 10,000,000 or more
   need a separate commercial license from Lightricks for commercial use of LTX-Video
   (LTX-Video Open Weights License, section 2). (c) Third-party material in examples/ and its adaptations (for example a
   sample video conditioned on a CC BY reference frame) follows that material's license and
   attribution file (…-ATTRIBUTION.md); this license does not limit the original author's
   attribution or the rights their license guarantees.
6. Outputs made under section 1 may be used only for the same personal learning purpose. Users are responsible for third-party rights in outputs. AI-generated video must
   not be presented as a real recording.
7. This license applies from the commit that contains this file. Versions published earlier
   under the MIT License remain under the MIT License for those who obtained them then.
8. Any breach automatically terminates all rights under this license; the user must stop
   using the Software and delete their copies. The copyright holder intends to claim
   damages for unauthorized use, educational use in breach of section 1-2, commercial use,
   modification and redistribution to the fullest extent permitted by applicable law,
   including actual damages, a reasonable license fee, profits gained from the breach,
   statutory damages, punitive or enhanced damages where the law allows them, and legal
   costs. Where an organization breaches, the claim may be made against the organization
   and against the persons who directed or knowingly allowed the breach.
9. The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The copyright holder is
   not liable for any damages arising from its use or inability to use it.
10. International scope, governing law and venue. (a) This license applies to every user
   worldwide. The Software is protected in the member states of the Berne Convention for
   the Protection of Literary and Artistic Works, the WTO TRIPS Agreement and the WIPO
   Copyright Treaty under their national laws. (b) This license is governed by the laws of
   the Republic of Korea, and the Seoul Central District Court has first-instance
   jurisdiction over disputes; the copyright holder may also bring claims in the courts of
   any country where an infringement occurs, under that country's law. (c) If a provision is
   invalid or unenforceable in a country, the remaining provisions stay in force and that
   provision applies to the fullest extent that country's law permits. (d) Downloading,
